TOOLCHAIN: llvm_aie-22.0.0.2026090201+a36c62b9, mlir_aie-1.4.2
SCOPE: compile only. No NPU, no hardware context. Verdicts are about the
  aie_api/Peano toolchain, never the silicon (see the docstring).

PRE-REGISTERED (written before the run, from the header listing):
  aie2: int8/uint8 x int4/uint4 compile; int4 x int8, int4 x int4 and int16 x int4 do not.
  aie2 control word: no intrinsic with a 4-bit A; 4-bit B only against 8-bit A.
  Gate A kills the aie_api/Peano DENSE path for int4 activations, W4A4 and W16A4 on aie2
  if those mmuls fail while their harness controls compile.
NOT PRE-REGISTERED: section 1's wrapper listing and section 3 were added after a dry
  run showed aie2p's int8 x int4 object containing unpack instructions. They are
  observations about how the toolchain lowers int4, not tested predictions.

