3. HOW aie_api LOWERS int8 x int4 PER TARGET (aie_api detail/<target>/mmul_8_4.hpp)
aie2: the compiler defines __AIE_ARCH__ = 20; mmul_8_4.hpp has no __AIE_ARCH__ branches
  __AIE_ARCH__ == (all): a 4-bit-B MAC control word (bmode 0) straight into the MAC; calls mac_4x16_16x8, mac_4x16_16x8_conf, mul_4x16_16x8  <- this target
aie2p: the compiler defines __AIE_ARCH__ = 21; mmul_8_4.hpp has __AIE_ARCH__ branches
  __AIE_ARCH__ == 21: the Peano intrinsic itself UNPACKS B to 8 bits, then 8-bit MACs; calls mac_4x16_16x16_conf, mul_4x16_16x16  <- this target
  __AIE_ARCH__ == 22: aie_api UNPACKS B to 8 bits, then an 8-bit MAC; calls mac_4x8_8x16_conf, mac_8x8_8x8_conf, mul_8x8_8x8
